& [StableArchitecture] is one versioned semantic walk
  + Planner projects candidate paths through objective, dependency, time, resources, effects, review, uncertainty, verification, stop, and reroute
  + Calendar preserves temporal proposals, authorized commitments, availability, deadlines, recurrence, wakes, reviews, misses, cancellations, completion, and provider-sync state
  + SemanticRepository preserves append-only material events, immutable content, snapshot generations, reference indexes, attribution, sensitivity, and retention
  + ChangeCapsule binds declared intent and admitted before state to candidate work, observed change, rear review, invalidation, Observer disposition, and admitted after state
  + prospective, execution, retrospective, and Observer-join lanes operate against exact immutable versions
  + CompilerWalk constructs forward and reviews rearward under the signed SMTC target and proof boundary
  = concise: plan forward, preserve the step, inspect backward, and release only the reconciled next step

& [PlannerAndCalendar] separate proposal from commitment
  + TaskContract binds purpose, principals, source and target scope, assumptions, invariants, authority requests, effects, completion, privacy, and retention
  + PlanRevision is an immutable candidate objective, dependency, temporal, effect, and review graph with alternatives and uncertainty
  + Schedule is a candidate allocation and never by itself a commitment
  + Commitment requires eligible authority and remains distinct from provider synchronization
  + CalendarItem has stable identity, immutable revisions, explicit kind, TaskContract, time, recurrence, dependencies, participants, authority state, lifecycle, provider-sync state, sensitivity, and disclosure
  + WakeCondition requests reentry and current-state validation rather than execution
  + Planner, Weaver, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Worker, user or policy, Calendar, rear review, and Observer each retain their distinct responsibility
  - never: derive priority, truth, urgency, authority, or consent from deadline, proximity, schedule, invitation, or provider state

& [TemporalData] is domain-aware and bitemporal
  + TimeExpression domain is civil, instant, monotonic, logical, valid, transaction, or uncertain
  + time value may be point, interval, duration, set, partial date, or symbolic condition
  + source, timezone and calendar when applicable, precision, interpretation, and uncertainty are explicit
  + valid time and transaction time are separate
  + conversions bind evidence and policy
  + recurrence is timezone-aware, exception-capable, horizon-bounded, and revision-preserving
  - never: infer causal order from timestamp, record position, left-right operand, filename, or digest alone

& [SemanticRepository] is event-sourced but not omniscient
  + RepositoryGeneration binds policy, exact predecessor frontier, admitted MaterialEvents, optional SemanticSnapshot root, derived index generation, Observer disposition, and digest
  + MaterialEvent records materially observable observation, decision, semantic transition, tool, effect, review, calendar, fault, admission, reentry, or compaction boundary
  + ContentObject preserves immutable bytes, digest, provenance, sensitivity, retention, and locators
  + SemanticSnapshot materializes a declared semantic event frontier with exact predecessor lineage
  + reference indexes are replaceable projections and cannot become semantic truth
  + GitProjection exports selected source and milestones as files, diffs, commits, branches, tags, or notes without replacing repository identity
  + branches and merges remain explicit
  - never: describe a sequential semantic snapshot as an atomic external-world snapshot

& [CaptureCadence] interprets every moment through materiality
  + task opening, admitted plan, semantic transition, tool boundary, effect boundary, review barrier, calendar commitment or trigger, yield, fault, reentry, completion, and selected milestone are durable candidates
  + high-frequency MicroEvents require liveness, fault, diagnosis, audit, or measurement purpose
  + aggregation declares coverage, source, method, count, loss, and rehydration status
  + expiry, compaction, redaction, and deletion declare authority and proof impact
  + materiality policy changes prospectively and cannot invent unobserved history
  - never: equate thoughtfulness with archive volume or require one commit per moment

& [ChangeCapsule] is the proof-bearing transition waist
  + stable change UUID and candidate generation
  + exact TaskContract, PlanRevision, RepositoryGeneration, and before snapshot
  + declared intent, target set, expected transform, permitted effects, proof gate, and unrelated-state exclusion
  + optional prepared candidate, separate execution request and observed outcome, and candidate snapshot
  + physical, source, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, proof, and calendar DiffRecords
  + justification, support, requirement, and compiler-impact deltas
  + version-bound ReflectionReturn with evidence, objections, uncertainty, invalidation, and residual
  + ObserverJoin reconciliation and after snapshot only on admission
  + capsule lifecycle is opened, prepared, execution_requested, effect_observed, reflection_requested, reflection_returned, reconciled, admitted, rejected, reverted, compensated, or unresolved
  = must: preserve added, changed, removed, preserved, and unrelated surfaces separately
  = must: preserve failed and superseded capsule generations

& [DiffTaxonomy] prevents change-category collapse
  + PhysicalDiff describes byte, file, row, graph record, package, or external resource change
  + SourceDiff describes source artifacts and spans
  + SemanticDiff describes identity, context, relation, type, contract, state, authority, uncertainty, or lifecycle meaning
  + BuildDiff describes dependency, compiler, SemanticIR, index, artifact, package, or invalidation
  + BehavioralDiff describes observable evaluation or interaction
  + EffectDiff describes proposed, authorized, denied, committed, failed, compensated, or observed external state
  + ProofDiff describes requirement, fixture, evidence, diagnostic, support, confidence, or completion claim
  + CalendarDiff describes estimate, schedule, commitment, trigger, delay, miss, recurrence, cancellation, or completion
  + every diff binds before and candidate subjects, derivation, independent evidence when required, completeness, invalidation, loss, and unknowns

& [BidirectionalLanes] coordinate without hidden shared state
  + ProspectiveLane prepares candidates from admitted versions
  + ExecutionLane performs only separately authorized work against a pinned version and returns observations
  + RetrospectiveLane reviews one exact capsule generation against preserved intent and evidence
  + ObserverJoin validates versions and returns and owns successor disposition
  + LaneCursor binds lane, task, repository generation, plan, capsule, dependencies, authority request, state, lease, timeout, and last message
  + LaneMessage is immutable and binds sender, receiver, subject version, payload, acknowledgment, causal predecessors, logical time, and expiry
  + PreparedAhead permits draft, retrieval, simulation, compilation, or staging while dependent admission and effects remain blocked
  + ReleaseBarrier opens only for the exact named dependent set after applicable review and version checks
  + CompareAndAppend rejects stale predecessor, generation, dependency, plan, target, or authority
  + bounded lag profiles declare eligible work, maximum count or duration, consequence, rollback, overdue behavior, and authority
  + timeout, cancellation, residual, crash reentry, and typed fault prevent indefinite blocking
  - never: exchange private chain-of-thought, hidden activations, K/V cache, or a shared mutable canonical state

& [WalkingAttentionFidelity] is cited behavior without authority inheritance
  + selected external repository is C:\Project\WalkingAttention at branch codex/walking-attention-pulse and commit 35d24b9245dbf1625dd20e29860e943981f65300
  + selected forward, rear, tandem, and controller files were tracked and clean with exact bytes and SHA-256 recorded in the fidelity artifact
  + 584 unrelated dirty entries were excluded and untouched
  + forward input, interface, attachment, diff, meaning, fault, frame, and seed map to prospective records
  + rear declared intent, actual diff, deltas, fault, completion gate, and refusal map to retrospective records
  + tandem send, receipt, return, named release, timeout, and checker refusal map to LaneMessages and ReleaseBarrier
  + reentry maps to versioned continuation state
  + the selected controller explicitly states unsigned_sjs_candidate_supporting_exchange_ledger_checker
  + CTPR owns its derived canonical behavior and does not claim a valid external signature
  - never: import hidden attention, private reasoning, raw heatmaps, consciousness, fixed pulse pacing, automatic message sending, runner mutation, prompt artifacts as release authority, or unrelated dirty state

& [CompilerWalk] applies CTPR to the signed SMTC fabric
  + CompilerGeneration binds source, dependencies, LanguageProfile, compiler, SemanticIR root, targets, correspondence, loss, diagnostics, proof, and lifecycle
  + forward stages are source_pinned, parsed, resolved, lowered, and projected
  + rear reviews are source_diffed, semantic_diffed, impact_analyzed, correspondence_checked, and proof_checked
  + CompilerImpact propagates change to IR, indexes, packages, schedules, workflows, models, tool schemas, and hardware projections
  + target generation cannot be its only correspondence evidence
  + Observer reconciles forward result and rear evidence before any package-family admission
  + this specification implements no compiler and grants no runtime package authority

& [BackwardLearning] changes future candidates without rewriting history
  + ForecastError compares preserved estimate and actual observations
  + PlanDeviation records skipped, inserted, reordered, blocked, repeated, or abandoned steps
  + SemanticSurprise records a meaning, dependency, identity, or boundary exposed through actual work
  + LessonCandidate binds source capsules, proposed future use, scope, counterexamples, confidence, review, invalidation, and rollback
  + TrainingExampleCandidate additionally binds redaction, consent, sensitivity, label provenance, evaluation split, and admission state
  + adoption requires a new reviewed SOP, policy, estimate, routine, or corpus generation
  - never: make later knowledge appear in the original plan or promote one review directly into training data

& [PrivacyAndRetention] are field and purpose scoped
  + sensitivity classes are public, project_internal, personal, confidential, secret, credential, regulated, and unknown_sensitive
  + calendar title, participants, location, routine, availability, and notes may differ in sensitivity
  + source, diff, prompt, provider payload, tool result, trace, proof, index, embedding, and lesson are independently classified
  + relevance and index access do not authorize protected-source disclosure
  + retention records minimum proof need, maximum operational retention, archive, compaction, redaction, deletion authority, and tombstone lineage
  + Git and semantic-repository retention remain separate

& [ECSProjectionBoundary] records the new alternative accurately
  + ECS entity may project a stable semantic subject into a runtime handle
  + component may project a typed immutable facet
  + system may project a compiler pass, faculty operation, planner, validator, review, join, or effect gate
  + system schedule may derive from Planner dependencies and declared access sets
  + command buffer may hold proposed changes until Observer or EffectBroker admission
  + contextual, temporal, n-ary, provenance, truth-status, authority, and proof relations remain canonical semantic data
  + component presence, archetype membership, system registration, and cache locality prove no semantic claim or authority
  + ECS is not selected; a later profile must measure correspondence, replay, speed, memory, proof overhead, and graph-only fallback

& [DeterministicFallback] is mandatory
  + logical time, local Calendar representation, event journal, ChangeCapsule validation, lane protocol, rear review, Observer disposition, compiler diff inputs, and replay remain expressible without model or provider
  + absent, stale, uncertain, rejected, failed, or disabled model and provider states are visible
  + no planned deadline or review depends on a provider-only hidden state

& [FaultAndProofSet] is explicit
  + faults include calendar_as_plan, false_urgency, time_domain_collapse, moment_flood, snapshot_overclaim, history_rewrite, rear_rationalization, forward_runaway, reflection_deadlock, shared_mutation_race, stale_release, lost_return, diff_surface_collapse, unrelated_diff_mix, compiler_self_certification, calendar_privacy_leak, unsigned_external_authority_claim, and ECS_semantic_flattening
  + deterministic proof rejects stale versions, unsourced time, mixed unrelated diff, missing reflection, fabricated atomic snapshot, history rewrite, hidden effect, invalid lane order, missing receipt, invalid recurrence, privacy overprojection, and self-certified target
  + negative and no-benefit results remain valid evidence

& [EvaluationSet] measures thoughtfulness, not volume
  + planning quality is feasibility, dependency satisfaction, deadline fit, slack, uncertainty, and correction rate
  + reflection quality is detected overreach, underreach, missing proof, requirement discovery, and false-positive rate
  + semantic diff quality is identity, relation, contract, authority, effect, and target impact precision and recall
  + join quality is stale rejection, invalidation, release, no deadlock, and deterministic replay
  + calendar quality is timezone, recurrence, commitment, wake, miss, cancellation, reschedule, and provider divergence handling
  + history quality is completeness, attribution, unrelated-state separation, compaction fidelity, privacy, and inspectability
  + work cost is journal volume, snapshot amplification, review latency, blocked forward time, compiler work, storage, and user attention

& [FirstImplementationFrontier] is pure forms only under separate claim
  + immutable definitions for every conceptual and logical record
  + normalized deterministic serialization
  + pure structural and semantic validation
  + malformed and illegal-state negative fixtures
  + no service, clock, filesystem, Git, provider, database, thread, calendar, notification, model, tool, desktop, hardware, or external effect
  + later deterministic logical-time runtime fixture remains blocked until pure forms and its own exact dependencies pass

& [RequirementSet] is canonical
  + CTPR-001 through CTPR-038 are individually mapped in the requirement matrix
  + semantic and logical specification status is satisfied after phase-lock validation
  + pure forms, deterministic runtime fixture, live providers, concurrency, persistence, ECS, training, Operator Shell, and hardware remain not started

